# TypeCount landing — cache policy
#
# Goal: a normal refresh (or even just navigating back to the site) must show
# the newest deploy. No hard refresh should ever be required.
#
# The previous policy set max-age=3600 on /style.css and /app.js, so returning
# visitors kept executing hour-old JavaScript for up to an hour after a deploy.
# Now everything that carries behaviour revalidates on every request.
#
# Revalidation is cheap: Cloudflare sends an ETag (a hash of the file), so a
# cookie-less 304 round trip is all a cached visitor pays. When the file has
# changed, the new bytes come down immediately.
#
# Only the two brand images, whose filenames do not change but whose content
# almost never does, get a long cache.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Brand images: long cache, they are effectively immutable.
# `! Cache-Control` detaches the /* value first, otherwise Cloudflare joins the
# two rules into "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=604800",
# and RFC 9111 says a duplicated directive resolves to the first — i.e. the
# long cache would silently not apply.
/assets/typecount-mark.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/assets/icon.svg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Metadata — short cache, detached so the /* value does not duplicate it.
/robots.txt
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/sitemap.xml
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
